{{if .content_provider.Doc -}}
## Description
{{ .desc }}

{{end -}}

{{ if eq .plugin.Name "blackstork/builtin" -}}
The `{{ .name }}` content provider is built into the BlackStork engine. It is available out-of-the-box and requires no installation or dependency declaration.
{{ else -}}
## Installation

{{"{{"}}< hint note >{{"}}"}}
**BlackStork SaaS:** Plugin dependencies are resolved automatically by the platform. You do not need to install plugins or define the `blackstork` configuration block manually.
{{"{{"}}< /hint >{{"}}"}}

To use the `{{ .name }}` content provider locally via `blackstork-cli`, you must declare the `{{ .plugin.Name }}` plugin as a dependency in your global configuration block.

```hcl
blackstork {
  plugin_versions = {
    "{{ .plugin.Name }}" = ">= {{ .plugin.Version }}"
  }
}
```

After declaring the dependency, execute `blackstork-cli install` to fetch the plugin. See [Configuration]({{"{{"}}< ref "configs.md#global-configuration" >{{"}}"}}) for details.
{{ end }}
## Configuration

{{ $ctx := . -}}
{{with .content_provider.Config -}}
This content provider accepts the following configuration arguments within a `config content {{ $ctx.name }}` block:

```hcl
{{ renderDoc . "config" "content" $ctx.name -}}
```
{{ else -}}
This content provider does not accept any configuration arguments.
{{ end }}
## Usage

{{with .content_provider.Args -}}
This content provider accepts the following arguments within a `content {{ $ctx.name }}` block:

